---
/* Component — CardText
 * Quiet muted body text inside a card.
 *
 * Named CardText rather than CardDescription because it is not one description
 * per card: across apps/preview's 140 uses, 22 cards carry several and one
 * carries ten. It is repeating body copy, which is why it cannot be a
 * description prop on Card, and why it is a component rather than plain markup
 * in the body slot — slotted content never carries the scope attribute, so it
 * would render unstyled.
 *
 * Typography is transcribed from card.css's .card-description, built from the
 * same semantic tokens; see Card for why the declarations live here rather than
 * referencing that class.
 *
 * Nothing rendered here carries a class, so a consumer's own <p> in the card's
 * body slot is untouched by the rule below. */
---

<p>
  <slot />
</p>

<style>
  p {
    font-family: var(--bravoixr-font-body);
    font-size: var(--bravoixr-text-body);
    font-weight: var(--bravoixr-weight-body);
    line-height: var(--bravoixr-leading-prose);
    color: var(--bravoixr-color-text-muted);
    /* Symmetrical, so flow-agnostic — kept as the source's shorthand. Spacing
     * between consecutive CardText comes from the card's own flex column. */
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
